    "faq_section_bjxzKR": {
      "type": "faq-section",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_4VGV9b": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is Mounjaro safe? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Mounjaro has been through rigorous clinical trials and is licensed in the UK for effective weight management in adults. It's approved by NICE (the National Institute for Health and Care Excellence) and has one of the most conclusive evidence bases of any weight-loss medication currently available. <\/p><p>As with all medications, it isn't suitable for everyone, which is why a thorough clinical assessment is an essential part of every settlehealth prescription. The most commonly reported side effects are gastrointestinal related and tend to ease as your body adjusts to treatment. Your clinician will review your full health history before prescribing and will support you throughout your treatment.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_bzzp7L": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does Mounjaro take to work? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Many people notice a reduction in appetite and cravings within the first few weeks of starting Mounjaro. Weight-loss changes typically become visible between four and eight weeks, with more significant results building over three to six months.<\/p><p>Mounjaro is introduced at a low starting dose and increased gradually — up to a maximum of 15mg — to allow your body to adjust comfortably. The results build with consistency over time, and your clinician will support you through every stage of that process.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_C9p89w": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is the difference between Wegovy and Mounjaro? ",
            "row_content": "<p>Both are clinically proven weight-loss medications that are injected weekly. But they work differently. Wegovy contains semaglutide, which mimics the single hormone glucagon-like peptide (GLP-1) to reduce cravings and help you feel fuller for longer. Mounjaro contains tirzepatide, which targets the two hormones GLP-1 and glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) simultaneously to slow digestion, reduce appetite and help you feel fuller for longer. <\/p><p>Individual results vary with both medications. The right choice depends on your health history, your body and your goals. And that’s what we’re here for. Your clinician will assess this during your consultation to find the most effective medication for you. <\/p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_VqL7ez": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "disabled": true,
